// A second declaration of a file-scope variable is the same object, not a new
// one: `extern int y[2];` then `int y[2] = { 7, 9 };` is one row, and the
// definition's initializer and type are the ones that count. Each pass of the
// emitter looks a name up by its first row, so a second row would have its
// initializer stored where nothing reads it.
